ARTEX — ABOVE THE STORM
(Final Structured Concept)

High volume.
Massive.
Controlled.
No chaos. No destruction.

25s Cinematic Structure
Storm + Multi-angle + Sec 14 Ionization Event
0–4s — ORBITAL SILENCE
Wide trailing shot.
Earth curvature fills lower half.
Massive thunderstorm system rotating below.
Lightning flickers deep inside cloud towers.
Ship drifting. Engines idle.
Low sub rumble begins.

5–8s — FULL BURN IGNITION
Rear close-up.
Main engines ignite in stable, white-hot plume.
Sound:
Deep sub impact + metallic engine roar.
Lightning cracks below half a second later.
Camera vibrates slightly — thrust-driven inertia only.

9–12s — TRAJECTORY REVEAL
High-altitude wide shot.
Ship carving arc across the planet’s limb.
Faint trajectory streak appears — subtle plasma trace.
Storm system beneath rotates slowly.
Thunder layered into audio.

13–16s — FRONT VECTOR + IONIZATION EVENT (Key Moment)
Camera ahead of ship, facing engines.
Earth horizon behind.

At 14s:
A micro shockwave ripple propagates along the upper atmosphere.

Not explosion.
Not blast.

A thin, circular compression ripple
— barely visible
— shimmering through the limb

Horizon line emits faint ionization glow
soft blue-white edge illumination

Lightning flashes inside storm exactly on sub pulse.
Audio peaks here.
Engine burn steady. No fluctuation.

17–20s — GOD SHOT ABOVE STORM
Top-down angle.
Storm eye below — rotating structure.
Lightning veins branching.
Ship cutting across in perfect line.
No wobble. No chaos.
Pure vector dominance.

21–23s — HULL PASS
Camera skims along hull.
ARTEX logo illuminated by lightning flicker.
Heat shimmer distorts storm reflection.
Metal surface shows wear and detail.
Engine burn continues uninterrupted.

24–25s — WIDE RESOLVE
Extreme wide.
Storm raging below.
Atmosphere faintly glowing from compression ripple aftermath.
Ship still burning.
No cutoff.
No drop.
Title fades in minimal:
ARTEX 

Audio Architecture (High Volume But Controlled)
No voice over, noly background music, SFX, and FX.

Layer stack:

• Deep industrial engine roar (continuous)
• 110–115 BPM PHONK sub pulse
• Low orchestral brass swell at 13–16s
• Distant thunder layered rhythmically
• No melodic hook

Peak at 14–16s.
Then sustain.

No emotional collapse.

Just mass.